## 🔵 Canonical NOR Constructions (clean RDG‑style)

### 1. **NOT**  
Tie inputs together:

```
A ----+---- NOR ---- Q = ~A
      |
      +----
```

\[
Q = \text{NOR}(A,A) = \neg(A)
\]

---

### 2. **BUFFER**  
Double inversion:

```
A ---- NOR ---- NOR ---- Q = A
       (tied)   (tied)
```

\[
Q = \neg(\neg A) = A
\]

---

### 3. **OR**  
NOR then invert:

```
A ----+
      +---- NOR ---- NOR ---- Q = A+B
B ----+         (tied)
```

\[
Q = \neg\neg(A+B) = A+B
\]

---

### 4. **AND**  
Invert inputs, then NOR:

```
A ---- NOR ----+
       (tied)  +---- NOR ---- Q = A·B
B ---- NOR ----+
       (tied)
```

\[
Q = \neg(\neg A + \neg B) = A\cdot B
\]

---

### 5. **NAND**  
AND then invert:

```
A ---- NOR ----+
       (tied)  +---- NOR ---- NOR ---- Q = ~(A·B)
B ---- NOR ----+         (tied)
       (tied)
```

\[
Q = \neg(A\cdot B)
\]

---

### 6. **XOR**  
Build the two terms \(A\neg B\) and \(\neg A B\), then OR them:

```
A ----------------+---- NOR ----+
                  |             |
B ---- NOR -------+             +---- NOR ---- Q
       (tied)     |             |
A ---- NOR -------+---- NOR ----+
       (tied)     |
B ----------------+
```

\[
Q = A\neg B + \neg A B
\]

---

### 7. **XNOR**  
Invert XOR output:

```
(XOR circuit) ---- NOR(tied) ---- Q_xnor
```

\[
Q_{\text{xnor}} = \neg Q_{\text{xor}}
\]

---

Fundamentals
  NOR(A,B) = ~(A OR B) = ~A AND ~B
  Output is 1 only when both inputs are 0
  Any Boolean function can be built from NOR alone
  (De Morgan + inversion staging)

Variables
  A, B : inputs
  Q    : output
  ~    : NOT / inversion

------------------------------------------------
NOT  (inverter)
  Tie both NOR inputs together

  A ----+---- NOR ---- Q = ~A
        |
        +----

  Q = NOR(A,A) = ~(A+A) = ~A

------------------------------------------------
BUFFER
  Two NOTs in series (double inversion)

  A ---- NOR ---- NOR ---- Q = A
         (tied)   (tied)

  Q = ~~A = A

------------------------------------------------
OR
  NOR followed by a NOT (cancel the outer inversion)

  A ----+
        +---- NOR ---- NOR ---- Q = A+B
  B ----+         (tied)

  First  NOR gives ~(A+B)
  Second NOR (tied) inverts it back to A+B

------------------------------------------------
AND
  Invert both inputs, then NOR them
  (De Morgan: A AND B = ~(~A OR ~B))

  A ---- NOR ----+
         (tied)  +---- NOR ---- Q = A·B
  B ---- NOR ----+
         (tied)

  Q = NOR(~A, ~B) = ~(~A + ~B) = A·B

------------------------------------------------
NAND
  AND followed by a NOT
  (or invert the AND output)

  A ---- NOR ----+
         (tied)  +---- NOR ---- NOR ---- Q = ~(A·B)
  B ---- NOR ----+         (tied)
         (tied)

  Q = ~(A·B)

------------------------------------------------
XOR  (A XOR B = A~B + ~A B)
  Build the two AND terms, then OR them

  A ----------------+---- NOR ----+
                    |             |
  B ---- NOR -------+             +---- NOR ---- Q
         (tied)     |             |
  A ---- NOR -------+---- NOR ----+
         (tied)     |
  B ----------------+

  Intermediate:
    ~A, ~B from tied NORs
    A~B and ~AB from the middle NORs
    Final NOR pair ORs those terms

------------------------------------------------
XNOR  (equivalence: ~(A XOR B))
  Same as XOR with one extra inversion on the output
  (or use A B + ~A ~B)

  Take XOR circuit above, add one more tied NOR on Q
  Q_xnor = ~Q_xor


